      "writtenOn": "2022-04-08T23:43:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "One way of using build time macros is to create an array property in the cros-ec,gpio-led-pins or cros-ec,pwm-led-pins, instead of iterating through the nodes which will result in duplicates (same LED-ID for different nodes) and might not be very straightforward with macros.\n\n  / {    \n          gpio-led-pins {    \n                  compatible \u003d \"cros-ec,gpio-led-pins\";    \n      \n                  led-id \u003d \"EC_LED_ID_BATTERY_LED\", \"EC_LED_ID_POWER_LED\";\n \n                  color-off {    \n                          led-color \u003d \"LED_OFF\";    \n                          led-id \u003d \"EC_LED_ID_BATTERY_LED\";    \n                          led-pins \u003d \u003c\u0026gpio_ec_chg_led_y_c1 0\u003e,    \n                                  ┆  \u003c\u0026gpio_ec_chg_led_b_c1 0\u003e;    \n                  };    \n      \n                  color-amber {    \n                          led-color \u003d \"LED_AMBER\";    \n                          br-color \u003d \"EC_LED_COLOR_AMBER\";    \n                          led-id \u003d \"EC_LED_ID_POWER_LED\";    \n                          led-pins \u003d \u003c\u0026gpio_ec_chg_led_y_c1 1\u003e,    \n                                  ┆  \u003c\u0026gpio_ec_chg_led_b_c1 0\u003e;    \n                  };    \n      \n                  color-blue {    \n                          led-color \u003d \"LED_BLUE\";    \n                          br-color \u003d \"EC_LED_COLOR_BLUE\";    \n                          led-id \u003d \"EC_LED_ID_BATTERY_LED\";    \n                          led-pins \u003d \u003c\u0026gpio_ec_chg_led_y_c1 0\u003e,    \n                                  ┆  \u003c\u0026gpio_ec_chg_led_b_c1 1\u003e;    \n                  };    \n          };    \n  };",
